{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Mourns.</b> The word ארץ (land) is found in masculine, like נעתם ארץ (Isaiah 9:18). Now this verse contradicts the words of R. Moses the Cohen, who said that תאכלהו אש לא נפח (Job 20:26) is the way of the language: every word that is both masculine and feminine, one cannot use feminine language after masculine language." "<b>Has become parched.</b> Refers to the king of Assyria, for it is an active verb, until it withers — that is, is cut down." "<b>Has become like Sharon.</b> Like חבצלת השרון (Song of Songs 2:1)." "<b>And is shaken out.</b> From the root of ככה יהיה נעור ורק (Nehemiah 5:13)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The verse citation in the first example reads נעתם ארץ; the standard text of Isaiah 9:18 has נעתם ארץ, confirmed as matching."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:30.481572757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}